{#
  _ca_bundles.j2 — the SINGLE renderer for a CA file's read-only bind mount.

  A connection's `tls.ca_bundle` names a file on the host, and a container
  reads it at the SAME path, so the key names one file on the host and inside.
  Every compose template that hands a container such files imports this macro
  rather than writing the mount itself, so the escaping cannot drift between
  them.

  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  IMPORTING AND WHITESPACE
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

  A plain (context-free) import, as for `_network_axis.j2` beside it:

      {% import "services/_ca_bundles.j2" as ca %}

  The web-terminal stack's renderer searches the templates root after its own
  directory, so its template imports by the same path.

  The macro emits a LEADING newline before each entry and no trailing one, and
  is called alone on its own line inside a `volumes:` list with a left-trim
  marker:

      {{- ca.mounts(connection_ca_bundles) }}

  An empty or undefined list renders nothing, and the line disappears.

  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  WHAT AN EDIT HERE REDDENS
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Every importer's render is pinned byte for byte, so an edit to the macro
  moves the goldens of every importer at once. Regenerate in the same change:

      PYTHONPATH=src ./.venv/bin/python tests/templates/test_render_defaults_golden.py
      PYTHONPATH=src ./.venv/bin/python tests/templates/test_render_axis_shapes.py
#}

{#- One read-only bind per path, in the long syntax so any path is carried
    whole. `$` doubles to `$$`, so compose reads a path literally rather than
    interpolating it; `tojson` quotes it for YAML. -#}
{%- macro mounts(paths, indent=6) -%}
{%- set pad = ' ' * indent -%}
{%- for path in paths | default([], true) -%}
{%- set quoted = path | replace("$", "$$") | tojson -%}
{{ ['', pad ~ '- type: bind', pad ~ '  source: ' ~ quoted, pad ~ '  target: ' ~ quoted, pad ~ '  read_only: true'] | join('\n') }}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- endmacro %}
